// ---- Passages
pass('pax11', 'Passage: a root section', 'A thin section of a root shows an outer layer with unicellular hairs, then a cortex of parenchyma, then a single ring of barrel-shaped cells whose walls have a band of suberin. Inside this is a layer from which side roots arise. The xylem forms a star with four arms, and phloem patches alternate with the arms. The pith is tiny.');
pq('pax11', 3, 'root', 'The ring of barrel-shaped cells is the', 'endodermis', ['epidermis', 'pericycle', 'hypodermis'], 'The Casparian strip of suberin is a feature of the endodermis.');
pq('pax11', 4, 'root', 'The section is from a', 'dicot root', ['monocot root', 'dicot stem', 'monocot stem'], 'A four-armed xylem (tetrarch) and tiny pith are dicot root features.');
pq('pax11', 5, 'root', 'During secondary growth of this root, the first cambium appears', 'as strips below the phloem bundles', ['as a ring in the cortex', 'within the endodermis', 'at the root cap'], 'The conjunctive tissue below phloem becomes cambial strips.');
pass('pax12', 'Passage: two stems', 'Stem S has vascular bundles in a ring, each with a strip of cambium between xylem and phloem. The cortex has a collenchymatous hypodermis and a starch sheath. Stem T shows scattered vascular bundles, each surrounded by a sclerenchymatous sheath, and the ground tissue is not divided into regions.');
pq('pax12', 3, 'stem', 'Stem S is', 'a dicot stem', ['a monocot stem', 'a monocot root', 'a gymnosperm needle'], 'A ring of open bundles with cambium is dicot.');
