mc(4, 'complex', 'Which of the following has both a nucleus and living contents?', 'Companion cell', ['Vessel', 'Tracheid', 'Xylem fibre'], 'Companion cells are living with nuclei. The others are dead.');
mc(4, 'complex', 'Which of the following is correct about vessel elements and tracheids?', 'Vessel elements have perforations at the end walls', ['Tracheids have perforated end walls', 'Both are living', 'Both are phloem cells'], 'Vessels are a long cylindrical tube-like structure made of many cells with perforated end walls.');
mc(4, 'complex', 'The tissue that is mainly responsible for transport of organic food in a mature angiosperm stem is', 'phloem, through sieve tubes', ['xylem, through vessels', 'cambium', 'cork'], 'Sieve tubes conduct organic solutes.');
mc(4, 'complex', 'Which of the following is a living cell of phloem and is also the cell which carries out the actual conduction in angiosperms?', 'Sieve tube element', ['Companion cell', 'Phloem fibre', 'Tracheid'], 'Sieve tubes carry the sugars. Companion cells help but do not carry out the bulk conduction.', 'Companion cells are living too.');
